  (text "Rackglow - WT32-SC01 Plus + MSGEQ7 spectrum analyser" (at 25.4 27.94 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fd6e51ba-f542-4bdf-90eb-4d72781abb6a"))
  (text "MSGEQ7 support parts are the datasheet Typical Application: 22k + 0.01uF into IN,\n0.1uF on VDD (CD) and on pin 6 (CG), 200k from CKIN up to VDD and 33pF from CKIN\ndown to GND (165 kHz clock)." (at 25.4 35.56 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "946ba706-826c-49ce-9be3-c41850d73a49"))
  (text "J1 takes a Eurorack-level FX send (~10 Vpp). The MSGEQ7 wants roughly\n0.1-0.3 Vpp, so RV1 on the front panel attenuates: set it so the loudest\npassage just reaches the top band without pinning." (at 96.52 111.76 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "88d01030-b206-406c-922d-c0910bf8a5e8"))
  (text "POWER - two options, fit one:\n\nJ3   Eurorack 10-pin bus: +5V and GND only. Confirm which pins\n     carry them on your bus board before wiring.\n\nJ4   External 5 V supply (screw terminal).\n\nThe LEDs are the load that matters: 145 LEDs (5 x 29) draw several\namps at full white, far beyond a Eurorack 5 V rail. Big case: external\nsupply on J4 feeds both the board and the LEDs. Small case (3 x 29):\nsame rule." (at 96.52 134.62 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9523516f-0214-4d81-ac25-9484331774ad"))
  (text "Strip layout is set in the web UI (strips x LEDs per strip), chained\non one data line with alternate strips reversed." (at 96.52 172.72 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bfe6ea30-debd-4a48-869b-966d1059964b"))
  (sheet_instances
    (path "/" (page "1"))
  )
